# 0.5: in a multi-section document every error line
# is re-based from its section-local number to the FILE line number — including
# a message that carries a newline.
#
# The re-basing pattern matched the message with `.`, which stops at a newline,
# so such a message failed the match and kept its section-local number: the
# line below was reported as Line 2 (its position inside section 2) instead of
# Line 20. The newline comes from the author: `"x\ny"` is a quoted value with
# the newline escape, and the RULE 2.4 diagnostic echoes the value verbatim.
#
# NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTERS. Because the message echoes a raw newline, this one
# diagnostic occupies TWO physical lines of the golden. The golden is the
# engine's error list sorted and joined with LF, so the bytes are exact; a
# subprocess harness that splits stdout on LF sees two lines, and they sort
# back into the same order because only one error is reported.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A"

figdown 0.5 block
node b "B" shape="x\ny"
